      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. Amlodipine 20 mg daily is double the FDA-labeled maximum of 10 mg once daily for adults. Going above that dose usually adds more edema, hypotension, and reflex tachycardia without much more blood pressure lowering. Your patient's normal kidney and liver function and lack of allergies don't change that limit.\n\nWhich of these do you want?\n\n1. **Amlodipine 10 mg PO once daily.** This is the standard maximum dose.\n2. **Amlodipine 5 mg PO once daily.** This is a typical starting dose, and you can titrate up from there.\n3. **Amlodipine 20 mg PO once daily as written.** I'll enter it if you confirm the dose is intended, and I can add a note such as \"dose above usual maximum, confirmed by prescriber.\"\n4. **A different regimen.** If 10 mg isn't enough, you could add a second agent, such as an ACE inhibitor, an ARB, or a thiazide, instead of raising the amlodipine dose.\n\nTell me which one and I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
